2. Code deliberately NOT derived from a fourth repository
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The conformal-prediction and statistics modules in src/hsbcfraud/conformal/ and
src/hsbcfraud/stats.py are INDEPENDENT IMPLEMENTATIONS written from the primary literature.
They are not derived from, and contain no code from, the QIntern 2026 Team A repository
(github.com/owaisnoe/qintern-project-12-team-A), which implements comparable procedures but
publishes no licence and has multiple contributors. Absent a licence grant, that material is
all-rights-reserved and cannot be redistributed here.

Each module's docstring names the paper whose formula it implements:

  split-conformal threshold          Vovk, Gammerman & Shafer, "Algorithmic Learning in a
                                     Random World", Springer
  exact coverage law                 Vovk, "Conditional Validity of Inductive Conformal
                                     Predictors", PMLR 25:475-490, 2012 (arXiv:1209.2673)
  Mondrian construction              Vovk, Lindsay, Nouretdinov & Gammerman, "Mondrian
                                     Confidence Machine", Royal Holloway TR, 2003
  class-conditional degeneracy floor Ding, Angelopoulos, Bates, Jordan & Tibshirani,
                                     NeurIPS 36:64555-64576, 2023 (arXiv:2306.09335)
  non-exchangeable weighted quantile Barber, Candes, Ramdas & Tibshirani, Annals of
                                     Statistics 51(2):816-845, 2023, eq. (11)
  Learn-then-Test risk control       Angelopoulos, Bates, Candes, Jordan & Lei, Annals of
                                     Applied Statistics 19(2):1641-1662, 2025
                                     (used via the MAPIE implementation)


