4. Optional dependency that changes the licence surface
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The `gpu-crosscheck` extra is NOT installed by `make venv` and is not required to reproduce
any reported number. It exists only for the four-way simulator agreement check (E11).

Installing it adds:

  qiskit-aer                    0.17.2    Apache-2.0
  qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11           0.17.2    Apache-2.0
  cuquantum-cu11 (transitive)             NVIDIA Software License Agreement -- PROPRIETARY

qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 declares a dependency on `cuquantum-cu11`, so installing the extra
brings NVIDIA's cuStateVec binary into the environment. That binary is not open source. The
NVIDIA Software License Agreement grants a royalty-free licence to install, use and
distribute the software, and permits commercial use; it prohibits reverse engineering,
modification and derivative works, prohibits use in a manner that would subject the software
to an open-source licence, excludes life-critical applications absent a separate agreement,
and caps NVIDIA's cumulative liability at USD 10.00.

This project therefore does not describe cuQuantum as open source, does not redistribute the
binary, and keeps it off the path that produces reported results. See docs/decisions.md
D-006 for why the production kernel path uses qiskit-machine-learning's
FidelityStatevectorKernel -- pure numpy, no Aer, no NVIDIA binary -- instead.


